      "id": "reindex-batch-size",
      "title": "Reindex: batch size",
      "question": "How do steady throughput, start-up and total time of the reindex job change with the number of images per model call?",
      "answer": "Steady throughput rises from 166 to 246 images/s between batches of 8 and 256, mostly because fewer, larger database writes leave the model busier (model time is flat from 64 on); start-up grows with the batch because one worker loads the whole first batch, so on 517 images total time is lowest around 32-64 and the default stays at 64.",
      "report": "reindex.md",
